{
  "explanation": "The attacker from IP 91.121.40.3 attempted multiple Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks by injecting malicious JavaScript payloads, including script tags, event handlers in SVG elements, and javascript URIs, into parameters like 'q', 'bio', and 'next'. The HTTP 400 status codes indicate that the web application successfully rejected or failed to process the malformed requests, preventing the execution of the payloads.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Initial Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement robust output encoding and contextual escaping for all user-supplied input rendered in the browser.",
    "Deploy a strong Content Security Policy (CSP) to restrict the execution of unauthorized inline scripts and external connections.",
    "Validate and sanitize all incoming parameters on the server side using allow-lists rather than block-lists."
  ]
}
